# Copy this file to .env (gitignored, never commit real values) and fill in the
# values below. Used by powershell-scripts/Get-AirtableExport.ps1.
#
# Full walkthrough, including how to get access in the first place:
#   docs/operations/SETUP.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AIRTABLE_API_KEY -- a Personal Access Token, despite the variable name.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The name is historical. Airtable removed the old "key..." API keys in
# February 2024; what you need now is a Personal Access Token starting "pat".
# If yours starts with "key", it is the deprecated kind and will not work.
#
# Before you can create one, you need an ADMIN ACCOUNT on the Login.gov CRM
# base. Request it from the Login.gov CRM team -- Peter Marks or Erin Duffy.
#
# Then: Airtable > profile avatar (top right) > Builder hub > Personal access
# tokens > Create new token.
#
#   SCOPES -- add both:
#     data.records:read    See the data in records
#                          (what the pull actually uses)
#     schema.bases:read    See the structure of a base, like table names or
#                          field types (needed to look up table IDs when a
#                          table is renamed -- see the note below)
#
#   ACCESS:
#     All resources        All current and future bases in all current and
#                          future workspaces
#
# Copy the token immediately -- Airtable shows it exactly once.
#
# WHY schema.bases:read MATTERS even though the pull doesn't use it: Airtable
# returns 403 for BOTH "no permission" and "table doesn't exist", so the two are
# indistinguishable. A table rename has already broken a pull here once
# ("Partner Accounts" became "Partners"). Without this scope you cannot list
# what the token can see, and a rename looks exactly like an auth failure.
AIRTABLE_API_KEY=pat...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AIRTABLE_BASE_ID -- the Login.gov CRM base.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is the real value; it is not a secret (base IDs appear in the browser URL
# whenever the base is open). The TOKEN above is the secret, which is why .env is
# gitignored.
AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=appCPBIq0sFQUZUSY
